<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demetrius II Aetolicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 275–229 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Demetrius II of Macedon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-ii-nicator">Demetrius II</a> Aetolicus was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> from 239 to 229 BCE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-ii-gonatas">Antigonus II Gonatas</a>. Most of his reign was spent in the Demetrian War against the Aetolian and Achaean Leagues, which allied against him. After his death <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and other Peloponnesian cities joined the Achaean League, and his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> Doson became guardian of his young son Philip V.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/demetrius-ii-aetolicus.jpg" alt="Demetrius II Aetolicus" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Demetrius_II_(Demetrios_II)_of_Macedon_bronze_drachma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
